WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.233
Of the

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.267
entire White House,

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.202
Donald Trump's former

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.603
White House press secretary.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.337
The violence

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.972
we saw yesterday at our nation's

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.440
capital was appalling.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.109
Didn't realize the full extent

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.343
of the violence at the Capitol

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.444
until she settled in

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.545
to eat a turkey sandwich

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.481
for lunch on January six.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.382
Kayleigh McEnany

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.183
telling the January six committee,

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.818
I initially went back to my office

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:19.486
to eat lunch

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.321
but I eventually turned up the volume

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.289
on Fox News.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:23.990
McEnany

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.592
saying she was still piecing together

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.293
what was playing out at the Capitol,

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.462
not merely sitting by as the attack

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.330
unfolded.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.531
I in no way, shape

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.133
or form would eat a turkey sandwich

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.234
if I thought the Capitol Hill

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.568
was being seized.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.202
How White House

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.404
Officials Learned of rioters

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:39.472
storming the Capitol on January six

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.607
Just one of the details

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.775
emerging as the House Select

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:42.575
Committee releases

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.511
new batches of transcripts from roughly

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.146
a thousand witness interviews.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.747
The Select Committee intends

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.149
to make public

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:51.751
the bulk of its non-sensitive records

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.553
before the end of the year.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.021
A separate transcript revealing

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.156
how the White House crafted

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:56.990
a press release

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.391
in December 2020

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.026
calling for the firing of anyone

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:00.627
who accepted

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:01.127
the election

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.495
result hours

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.064
earlier than Attorney General Bill

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.899
Barr had told the Associated Press

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.201
there was no widespread voter fraud,

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.736
according to the draft press release.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.171
Anybody that thinks there wasn't

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.672
massive fraud in 2020

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.541
election should be fired.

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:15.975
The press release was never sent,

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:16.810
and Barr resigned

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.545
from the White House later that month.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:19.712
Since then, he hasn't

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.314
held back in criticizing Trump's

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.315
election lies.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:23.516
I was

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.851
somewhat demoralized

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.419
because I thought, Boy,

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.421
if he really believes this stuff, he has,

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.424
you know, lost contact with with

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.227
he's become detached from reality.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.930
And I went into this and would

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.332
you know, tell him how crazy

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.167
some of these allegations were?

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.402
There was never

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.404
there was never an indication of

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:47.674
interest

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.410
in what the actual facts were.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.212
The trickle of transcript revelations

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.013
coming after the committee recommended

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.081
that the Justice Department

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.249
bring criminal charges

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.750
against former President Trump

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.852
there was a conspiracy

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.153
to defraud the United States

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.554
to exchange an honest

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.689
to goodness

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:03.890
presidential election

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.391
for a counterfeit election.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.292
Trump's legal team

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.161
downplaying the committee's findings.

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.363
The report itself is not of much value.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.332
It's written by politicians

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.666
for a political purpose

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.869
and dismissing its criminal referrals.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.370
Even as Trump faces scrutiny,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.339
from a DOJ special counsel

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.940
that is now investigating his attempts

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.042
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:23.510
I mean,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.044
the referral itself

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.646
is pretty much worthless.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.780
The Department of Justice

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.849
doesn't have to follow it.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.584
Now, the committee has, of course,

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.919
released its final report,

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:33.620
but they have released

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.554
just a fraction

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.022
fill of the underlying evidence

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:36.623
they put out.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.591
Fewer than 100 of their interview

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.826
transcripts so far.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:40.627
They interviewed roughly

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.794
a thousand witnesses.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.163
And we are expecting many,

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.063
many more transcripts,

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.131
many, many more tidbits

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.066
about how this all unfolded.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:47.467
That's good,

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.034
because I don't feel

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.235
like you've been very busy

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.437
the last couple of months, years,

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.038
decades.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.773
Sara Murray, great reporting, as always.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.041
Thank you so much.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:55.708
Let's discuss now

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.676
with former special assistant

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.511
to President George W Bush and USA Today

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.579
columnist Scott Jennings,

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:00.713
along with Democratic former

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.315
South Carolina state representative

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.584
Bakari Sellers. Guys, thanks so much.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.451
Welcome to the show.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.352
Scott,

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:06.920
the former

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.487
president railed

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:08.621
against the January six committee

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.355
after they referred him

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.256
to the Justice Department

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.391
for criminal prosecution.

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:12.592
One of his attorneys calls

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.860
the referrals worthless

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.762
and political noise.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:16.629
I don't ask this question

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.865
from a legal basis politically.

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.266
Are they are they just noise

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.000
or are they worthless?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.235
Or do they have something that

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.469
can actually resonate here?

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.105
Well, the lawyers say they're

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.674
worthless from a legal perspective

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:29.209
because the DOJ is going to do

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.244
whatever it's going to do outside of

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:32.111
what Congress says.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.313
But as a political matter,

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.148
obviously, this entire process,

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.783
this entire unfolding of this

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.051
has taken a

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.319
toll on Donald Trump

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.820
along with other things.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.156
But clearly, this is dragging him down.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.190
I mean, look at the polling.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.559
I mean, the nation has soured on Trump

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.827
even more than they already were.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.862
The Republican Party is souring on Trump.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.897
He's losing in head to head

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.899
matchups with Ron DeSantis.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:53.466
When you match him

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.168
up against Joe Biden in a rematch

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:57.737
that nobody wants, he's losing badly.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.905
So obviously this,

00:03:58.905 --> 00:03:59.739
along with everything else

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:00.273
he's got going

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.774
on, has taken a real

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:02.942
toll on him politically,

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.444
even if the legal aspects of it

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:07.113
here are less than important.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:07.380
Corey.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.548
Do you feel like

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:08.948
my sense

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.683
was part of the rationale for doing this

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.618
was to put pressure

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.952
on the Justice Department?

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:13.853
Do you feel like the just department

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:14.587
needs to act

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:15.588
on these criminal referrals

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.022
for the select

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:16.923
committee investigation

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.691
to be seen as worthwhile in the

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.592
eyes of the American people?

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:21.761
Well, first of

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.128
all, I'm not

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:23.563
sure you can actually put pressure

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:24.430
on Merrick Garland

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.598
and the Department of Justice.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:26.366
I think

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.500
this Department of Justice,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.434
compared to the one

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.870
that we've seen with Jeff Sessions

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.372
and Bill Barr,

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:32.972
and I can't remember

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:33.973
the guy who was there for

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:34.841
like a blink of an eye.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:36.175
He was there for like once a year.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:36.876
He met Whitaker

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.611
maybe I think it's his name.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.647
That was a more political Department

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.814
of Justice,

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.383
whereas this is a Department of Justice

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:44.884
that can't really be pressured.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:45.752
But what I can say

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.619
is that the information

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:47.820
this garner from the January six

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.756
committee does provide a roadmap

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.891
for the special prosecutor

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.360
to maybe, just maybe come with charges

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:56.396
from January 6th.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:57.330
I don't think Donald Trump

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.798
has that much legal jeopardy

00:04:58.798 --> 00:04:59.799
from January 6th.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.634
I do think that individuals around him

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.102
who obstructed justice

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.203
usually it's not the crime,

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.238
it's the cover up

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.606
have a great deal of exposure

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:07.740
from January six.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.242
I think that Donald Trump

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.610
has the most exposure field

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.111
from actually

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.913
taking a classified documents

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.181
down to Mar a Lago.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:15.748
I think that

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:16.983
when you see his handling

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.052
of those classified documents, that and

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.087
what's going on with Bennie Willis

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:23.256
and the Cat County, Georgia,

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:24.891
Fulton County, Georgia,

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:26.326
those are the cases that

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.428
that probably give him more exposure

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:30.096
than January six.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:32.265
Impressive recall of Matt Whitaker's

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:33.266
distinguished tenure

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:34.133
at the Justice Department.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.001
Scott,

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.769
there's a New York magazine cover story

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:37.470
which writes

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.738
about Donald Trump's 2024

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:40.573
campaign in an article provocatively

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:41.240
titled Trump

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.809
Sad, Lonely, Thirsty,

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:43.810
Broken Basically

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:46.245
Pretend Run for reelection.

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.147
Trump adviser tells Olivia

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.483
that this campaign, quote, It's

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:52.051
not there in this business.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:52.719
You can have it.

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:53.686
And have it's so hot

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.254
and it can go overnight

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.989
and it's gone and you can't get it back.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:58.791
I think we're just seeing it's gone.

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:00.960
The magic is gone.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.328
Is the magic gone

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:03.730
for the former president at this point?

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:06.799
Well, he's certainly losing altitude.

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:07.333
I mean, look,

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:07.800
he's he's

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.068
not without

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:11.170
things to build a campaign out of it.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:11.971
He's got money.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.473
He's got a cadre of advisers

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:14.474
who are fully dependent

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:16.642
upon him for their livelihoods.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.112
He's got people who want Donald Trump.

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.613
I mean, there is a base of people

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.481
inside the party

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:22.949
that would rather have Trump

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:24.183
than than anybody else.

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.785
So that's not an insignificant thing

00:06:25.785 --> 00:06:26.486
to start with.

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:28.321
But where he is lost

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:30.123
is that over the last

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:32.992
I mean, go back to 2016,

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.427
he backs into the presidency

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:36.195
and from that point forward,

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:37.563
losing in 2018,

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:40.767
losing in 20, 20, losing in 21, losing in

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.602
20 to all the legal stuff

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.003
that has come along.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:44.971
Every Republican out

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.606
there is carrying his bags

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:47.974
and those bags are getting heavier

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:48.641
all the time.

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:49.542
So why do you want to call it

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.544
losing magic or whatever

00:06:51.878 --> 00:06:52.812
It's just getting too,

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:53.713
too heavy to carry

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:54.814
Donald Trump's bags

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:56.249
because nobody wants to lose

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:58.351
to Joe Biden in 2024.

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.118
And that's what the

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:00.153
Republicans are coming

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:01.954
to terms with

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:02.221
and that's

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:02.655
why you see

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:03.890
people who look like winners

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:04.891
who feel like winners

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:06.392
like Ron DeSantis on the rise

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:06.793
and people

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:07.860
who've been losing

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.628
for a number of years

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:10.296
like Donald Trump thinking

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:11.898
you know Bakari the former president

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:14.133
is responding to the criticism on truth,

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:15.635
social writing.

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:17.270
We have almost two years to go.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.204
The rallies will be bigger

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:19.272
and better than ever.

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:19.906
But it's a little bit

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:21.574
early, don't you think?

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:24.110
Is it too early to judge this campaign

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.211
or do you see real

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:27.246
vulnerabilities based on everything

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:29.048
that Scott just laid out in detail?

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:30.183
To some degree,

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:32.885
Well, the two points I like to make,

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:34.020
first is

00:07:34.187 --> 00:07:35.521
I never counted Donald Trump

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.623
out of an election again in my life.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.158
Like I firmly believe

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:40.293
we should be on the second term.

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:42.295
Of the Clinton presidency.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:43.796
And so I was one of the many people

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:44.897
who was a prognosticator

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:46.799
and got paid good money to come up here.

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:48.634
And I was flat out wrong.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.136
So I'm not going to count him out.

00:07:50.136 --> 00:07:50.470
In fact,

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.904
his campaign was worse

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:54.073
then in 20, 15, 20, 16

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:56.476
than it is actually today.

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:57.944
There is a lot of stuff, like Scott

00:07:57.944 --> 00:08:00.112
said, for him to build on

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:01.347
I wish Donald Trump,

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:02.682
if he was actually going to be

00:08:02.682 --> 00:08:04.016
a good candidate, would simply say

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.485
Merry Christmas.

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:06.152
He would talk about

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:07.386
the joy of the New Year.

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:09.055
He would talk about the lessons learned

00:08:09.055 --> 00:08:10.056
and maybe even tweet.

00:08:10.056 --> 00:08:11.457
He has risen,

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:13.125
but he's not capable of doing that

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:14.794
and he hasn't changed.

00:08:14.794 --> 00:08:16.062
And if you do not change,

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:16.963
if you do not learn,

00:08:16.963 --> 00:08:17.964
if you do not have that,

00:08:17.964 --> 00:08:20.132
if you do not mature in politics,

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:21.868
you'll get beat every day of the week.

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:22.435
And he hasn't been

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:23.336
able to do those things.

